WEBVTT

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.600
The story until now.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.750
Even though the new government sent him to Holland in Europe to study tactics,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:15.510
their prevailing strategy was American-style shock and awe.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.180
Awaiting him was the expensive euro, making the base subway fare ¥1,000.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.560
Though he relied on the Japanese government's PR comics there,

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.940
the enviable starting enviable salary for a novice French comicker was 90 euros a page.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:29.100
"That's more than you'd make after ten years at a major company!  You should thank the stars of the Seine!"

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:34.510
Thinking such, Nozomu, holed up in Paris, sunk into depression, and searching for salvation, turned to the world of fantasy science.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:38.080
Amid the citizenry, he argued in Esperanto that the use of lamps would ruin the country,

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.420
and his selfmade steamboat, the Himiko, burned in the Seine.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:46.620
Turning his shame into springs, he gained notoriety among the nobility of London as the "Spring Man".

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.450
"Western powers, tremble before me!  My science will protect Asia!",

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.940
he declared, setting his sights on a UFO base in Pagotania.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:01:00.610
At that point, he received a telegram from his fatherland saying "Come home and marry Miyazaki Aoi."

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:31.730
Shocked that there were still no storyboards on editing day

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:31.900
Shocked that the art wasn't done by ADR day

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:32.060
Shocked that dubbing got pushed back a week

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:32.230
Shocked that some cuts weren't done on delivery day

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:32.400
Shocked that we finished the video on broadcast day

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:32.660
Shocked that it actually broadcast at the normal time

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.470
Can we meet up after class?

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:44.310
What do I do!? My heart isn't ready!

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.720
It's about the poster for the upcoming Reading Week.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:58.050
Should it be green on a white background, or white on a green background?

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.830
Well, um.  What are you talking about?

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:08.600
I told you I wanted to talk to you about something, right?
Aren't you planning to go to an art college?

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.720
When you're called out somewhere and you're sure someone's going to declare their love,

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.210
but nothing happens, <i>that's</i> a surprise!

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:20.410
The Japanese, who are deeply suspicious, tend to be more surprised when, in fact, nothing happens.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:24.310
As a result of things which don't happen, they are reverse surprised!

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:27.910
To illustrate, say that, on your birthday, you receive a phone call

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:30.080
We're all going drinking, c'mon!

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.320
from a friend.  You show up nonchalantly expecting to be celebrated.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:35.170
Thanks!

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:36.550
He's here, he's here!

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:37.720
You drink normally,

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.850
We're splitting the tab, your share's \3000.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:43.360
and say goodbye normally without anything happening.  That feeling.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.490
Laters.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.840
To me.  To me.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.840
That kind of reverse surprise!

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.140
That's miserable.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:53.580
Yeah, that definitely happens.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.530
Oh, Miss Chie.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:57.630
Just before elections, you get a phone call from a classmate

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:01.320
who you haven't seen in years and were never that close with.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:08.220
You just talk normally about the old days, and then hang up.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.620
Nothing happening is more of a surprise.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.930
Yeah, that's definitely shocking.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.700
Man, I'm hot.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:18.340
Let's hurry up and change.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:27.980
A plain white T-shirt!

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.350
There being nothing there is more surprising!

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.270
In this modern era where everything goes too far,

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.250
our destination is the point of no surprise!

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:37.320
When you get a call going "it's me, it's me!",

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:40.350
it's more of a surprise when, rather than a scam, it really is your grandson!

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:44.230
Recently, at concerts, it's more of a surprise when there isn't an encore!

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:48.570
When the Chuo line runs on time with no incidents, that's more of a surprise!

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:51.590
It's more surprising when things don't happen!

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:55.310
It's the feeling you get when watching a horror film, thinking "it's coming, it's coming",

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.730
but you end up being more surprised that nothing happens, right?

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.510
Hey, Teacher.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.080
Wanna come up and listen to a song?

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.040
Sure, why not?

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:13.020
Teacher's doing something serious!

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.100
Thanks, please come again.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:22.630
Teacher, did anything happen?

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.240
No, nothing at all.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.240
Nothing having happened is more surprising!

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.880
Hey, Sekiutsu.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:38.380
Japanese don't understand.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:44.390
How surprising the everyday peace in this country is.

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:49.770
You're right.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:52.330
What's up with that ending!?

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:59.440
You remembered.  They completely ignored it at school.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:04.350
Sorry for the reverse surprise.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:05.180
But it's okay.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:08.280
Are you happy now?

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:20.460
All the players have, all across the country, started their training season!

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:23.160
Is it already that time?

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.150
Training, huh.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:28.230
It's about time for us to start.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:28.400
I don't really have my licence

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:28.570
My hobby is collecting cicada shells

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:28.730
My scalp is-

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:28.900
I hit level 99

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:29.070
I can't do it

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:29.300
I'm sorry

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:42.680
Teacher is standing in front of the police box as if he's brooding over something!

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:46.780
I did it.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.290
Teacher, just what did you do!?

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:57.830
Nothing.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:58.900
But you just—!

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:01.530
No, that's...

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:03.570
Confession training!

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.490
It's confession training.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:09.910
Why do you have to train for that sort of thing!?

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:14.780
It's difficult to admit one's own mistakes.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.780
When that time comes, will you be able to confess?

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:21.290
There are many circumstances in which,

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:26.520
if you apologize for a crime the moment it's committed, it'll be over without becoming a big deal!

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:33.030
Modern Japanese, unable to admit their faults, require such training!

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:35.470
So, just what did you do?

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:39.850
I said, it's just confession training.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.340
What are you saying!?

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:42.570
Teacher!

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:45.980
If you're doing confession training, you've got to assume you've done a particular crime.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.810
It's image training!

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.870
An image of my crimes?

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:54.770
Biting a dog's ear

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:57.250
Writing down what people say in their sleep

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.680
I did it.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:04.290
You can't think of anything major, can you.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.230
Can you really call that confession training!?

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:12.100
I want greater crimes!  Ones that you regret from the bottom of your heart!

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:15.840
I...

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:18.580
I did it!

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:30.970
This is the first time I've seen such sublime confession!

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:32.690
I did it!

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:35.430
I wonder just what grand crime she's envisioning!

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:41.500
If you go for it when you still haven't warmed up...

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:52.180
Anyway, I'd like you all to make it through simultaneous confession training without any injuries.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:55.690
All right, you're all guilt-ridden.

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:57.680
I'd like you all to visualize your crimes.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:10.860
Your envisioned crimes are all over the place!  This will never work for synchronized confession.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.930
Everyone needs to get on the same page.

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:14.420
If you put it that way,

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:16.030
we've got to do -that-.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:19.540
I did it.

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:21.920
I used up the life insurance.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:25.510
I lured him to Minato, then took the glasses off.

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:28.190
I strangled with bandages.

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:31.580
I looted a corpse and brought the clothing to a pawnshop.

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:33.150
I split the earth.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:36.190
Just what kind of crimes against whom are you envisioning!?

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:42.190
Well, there's plenty of cases in which
synchronized confession would be better, but...

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:44.690
Hey.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:49.370
One person says something different, and the story changes back and forth.

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:52.940
If the story is inconsistent, it just throws more fuel on the fire.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:58.990
There's a standard for everyone having
what they're apologizing for straight and all together.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.510
Call this the "confession mark".

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:03.950
You just wanted to say that!

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:07.250
Isn't it naïve to lessen crimes just because they've been confessed to?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.050
If anything, it can be more annoying!

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.860
We're admitting to it!

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:16.960
We're going out!

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:19.630
How annoying!

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:21.160
Sry!

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:23.350
That's not a crime.

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.370
Though it may be capital.

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:30.240
Even if it isn't a crime, coming out with a secret can be thought of as confession.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:33.840
Huh?  Dad?

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:35.610
I'm confessing.

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:41.520
I'm confessing!

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:43.470
My newspaper is—

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.000
I'm confessing!

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:52.510
I'm shocked!

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.570
Yes...  It seems training in being confessed to is also required.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:01.060
Those who suddenly hear a confession may do something dangerous, too!

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.350
Confessing to an affair.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.700
Confessing one's tastes.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:07.970
Sorry, I've gotta go.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.920
Having someone admit to not being a virgin.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:16.420
For both those who do it and those who it is done to, confession training is important.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:18.480
An even less possible dream.

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:22.630
A letter on an arrow!

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:24.730
It says that confession training is forbidden!

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:29.210
If this permeates out, the whole world of comics will be at risk of destruction!

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:30.330
Why!?

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:33.970
Everyone.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:36.370
The perpetrator is among us.

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:37.070
It's me.

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:40.210
I did it!

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:44.450
So the story doesn't hold together...

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:47.290
If confession training continues to spread,

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:52.060
our precious Conan and Kindaichi will be able to solve things without getting their hands dirty, right?

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:56.790
We must continue training in order to take a load off the VIPs!

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:59.200
I may have said it,

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:03.600
but confession training will make all sorts of comics and films fall apart!

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:08.290
Let's start the first confession gymnastics!

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:12.610
It's already captured the hearts of the general public!

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.250
Just who is Ki—

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:15.210
I did it.

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:22.040
I'm confessing! This is the real me.

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:27.110
The world of comics has taken catastrophic damage from confession training!

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:28.590
It's not just the world of comics!

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.900
It's bad for all of Japanese society!

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:36.100
Nine-tenths of politicians have capitulated to corruption investigations, and the Diet has completely stopped!

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:40.350
Eight-tenths of manufacturers have admitted that their products are defective!

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:42.610
Treating their failure seriously with a recall!

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:49.910
The producer himself acknowledged how dull his projects are, and voluntarily stopping releasing film after film!

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:55.220
Everyone is confessing too much!  Japan is grinding to a halt!

00:12:55.220 --> 00:12:58.960
Now, you should confess too!  Confess!

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:01.330
I shall never confess!

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.200
I'll run until the statute of limitations lapses!

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.950
It's been a while, teacher.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:19.640
I can say this since the statute of limitations has lapsed.  I...

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:23.010
Teacher, I...

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:28.500
Grandma Kaere, whose grave is this?

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:30.720
No one's in particular.

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:35.930
What a touching story.

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:39.050
What's with this dramaticism?

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:43.810
It's Granny Normal.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:47.690
She's drinking kelp tea.

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:48.800
Like normal.

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:50.550
Let's go!

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:51.320
Yeah!

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:58.580
Don't call me normal!

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:14.100
A mystery train,

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:17.300
with an unknown destination.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:17.770
Will that law pass

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:17.940
Will there be a stay of execution

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:18.100
Is it better to have paid into one's pension

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:18.270
Is it better to have bought a bike than to ride the trains and busses

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:18.440
Will there be a fourth season

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:18.700
Does anyone read these subtitles

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:25.240
That's just to trick kids.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:31.070
There's no such thing as an unknown destination, is there?

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:33.690
It fits in with the schedules of other trains,

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:36.590
so its destination is set from the beginning.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:39.960
This world is full of things like that.

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:44.960
Excuse me, but you seem to be a teacher.

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:47.470
Can I get you to answer this survey?

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:52.970
I don't think so, but I don't really know.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:57.380
Don't you have something to say about it?

00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:58.670
There's nothing there.

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:04.420
I see, so it is.  Then what do you think the problem is with modern education?

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.070
"Education is dead."

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:07.990
Don't you just want me to say that?

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:11.140
Haven't you already made up your mind?

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:20.500
Lately, there's been many cases of questions asked with a predetermined answer.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:25.320
Leading questions, designed to reach one's conclusion, looking for not an opinion, only agreement...

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:31.370
Questions where you just want a particular answer.  Yes, just like this mystery train with its destination already fixed...

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:37.020
We fight every day now.

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:39.690
Should I break up with my boyfriend?

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:40.920
Break up with him?

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:43.520
If you don't like him, then shouldn't you?

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:47.760
Well, he's not really all that bad.  And...

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:49.630
Haven't you already come to a conclusion?

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:59.340
In terms of love, there really are people who ask even after they've made up their mind.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:02.340
Hi, I'd like to buy a TV,

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:05.840
but I'm not sure if I want a plasma or an LCD.

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:12.350
I see.  This plasma TV, currently our sale of the week, may be to your interest.

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:16.410
But don't plasmas use a lot of power?

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:19.300
They did.  Nowadays, they're about average.

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:24.630
And won't it heat up my room?  Also, I'm worried about it making a high-pitched noise.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:27.700
It looks like he's already made up his mind.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:30.940
I think maybe I should quit drawing it.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:32.510
Yes.  If you quit...

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:37.820
No, wait.  If I do, I haven't the foggiest what I'll draw next.

00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:43.980
And I have no talents other than drawing comics, so it'll be tough to find a job at my age.

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:43.980
Looks like he's already made up his mind.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:46.030
He looks so bitter.

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:46.990
Oh, chief editor!

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:49.300
Can you keep up with serialization?

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:51.630
Yeah, I'll keep trying a little bit longer.

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:55.460
I see.  But sometimes it's best to quit when you're ahead.

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:59.570
It's unlucky to lose freshness, both in writing and in reading.

00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:02.500
And it looks like he's already made up his mind, too.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:05.010
That's a bit too realistic.

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:08.020
I wonder if I should stop watching this anime.

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:09.340
Shouldn't you?  It's pretty dull.

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:14.410
Well, there's an interesting episode every once in a while.  If I don't watch, I'll feel like I've missed it.

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:15.620
You've already made up your mind!

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:18.830
To not accept any answer but the one you seek...

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:21.620
The world has become a little bit more disgusting.

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:24.630
Perhaps it's better to die.

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:25.860
If you want to die...

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:27.820
If you want to die, then give it a shot!

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:29.360
But my heart's not ready!

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:30.930
Wait, this is dangerous!

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:32.760
What if I had died!? {do not change}

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:37.300
Looks like you've already made up your mind.

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:43.040
I've come to understand that you have a voracious appetite for life, teacher.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:43.810
Wrong!

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:48.690
It's not that I want to live, it's that I most assuredly won't die! {*}

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:53.490
Disembarking?

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:56.220
This is a gigantic terminal.

00:17:56.220 --> 00:18:00.630
From here, mystery trains bound to many different destinations depart.

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:05.630
Get on, everyone!  With your opinions and actions, the destinations change!

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:10.640
Even if they say that train's destination is unknown, where it's going has been determined from the start.

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:18.880
It's for those who believe the youth of Shibuya are running wild, and set up TV interviews expressly for that opinion!

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:22.040
That night train's destination is determined.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:21.660
Night Train to Soichiro

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:26.960
No matter which arguments you make, its destination has to be Tahara Shoichiro's opinion: the Asanama Train!

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:30.900
Gathering information nearby based on the conclusion that he's the culprit! {referencing with sign an old video game where you're told the culprit and have to find evidence}

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:33.990
When they can't risk being discriminatory, they screen employees with tests. {I don't really like this much better, but I thought I'd guve you another option to play with.}

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:37.810
Mystery trains with their predetermined destinations have left me in despair!

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:46.960
Everyone wants to get on the train leading to their preconceived conclusion.

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:49.210
No, they ride them even if they shouldn't!

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:52.600
So you aren't gonna pay me back?

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:54.220
What do we do now, huh?

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.710
Well?  What do we do now?

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:02.570
Where's that train going?

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:06.330
After this it goes underground and becomes a subway.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.140
Then it reaches an underground station.

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:12.070
Even if we know its destination, it still becomes lost.

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:17.350
In this world, there are station names that aren't shown even if we know the destination!

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:22.210
Excuse me, from which terminal does the train to Paradise on Earth depart?

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:25.840
It used to depart from the furthest-left terminal,

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:29.020
but it's had so few passengers lately that it's been cancelled.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:34.570
It used to be packed full of students.  Who had all already made up their minds the same way...

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:40.220
...So, what do we do from here?

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:45.880
Teacher, how about finally deciding on a woman?

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:48.860
Hmm, that's right.

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:50.350
With whom should I—?

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:56.460
Haven't you already made up your mind?

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:00.640
...Yes.

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:09.200
This is an express train that only those who've made up their minds on weighty decisions can ride.

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:11.830
NEETs who've decided what to do next.

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:15.230
Politicians who've made difficult decisions about the nation's future.

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:16.690
Well, we've arrived.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:19.250
The terminal station— The terminal station—

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:21.880
Putting it Off—  Arriving at Putting it Off—

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:26.090
I've decided to put it off.

00:20:27.270 --> 00:20:29.410
That's not a decision!

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:33.690
Congratulaitons, everyone!   You've made a decision!

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:37.330
We've decided to think about it in two or three years!

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:41.200
I've decided to borrow from the next generation.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:46.120
To be honest, this is the most popular and well-used station.

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:49.260
I've decided to put off losing my virginity.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:52.530
I've decided to put off contributing to my pension fund.

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:55.540
I've decided to put off seeing a doctor.

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:06.780
It always happens after volume ten. No matter what you do.

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:45.650
The Zetsubou-sensei Drawing Song is about to start.

00:22:45.650 --> 00:22:48.020
Matching the song, let's draw together, okay?

00:22:49.580 --> 00:22:55.900
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:22:55.900 --> 00:23:02.370
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:03.950
Lightning...

00:23:03.950 --> 00:23:05.610
Flash!

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:07.090
Lightning...

00:23:07.090 --> 00:23:08.820
Flash!

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:12.020
The rain comes pouring down.

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:15.280
From the gaps came the leaks.

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:18.040
Two puddles were made.

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.600
Let's go fishing, there's the fish hook!

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:26.020
With the fish we caught, we made a fish cake.

00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:29.540
It's Zetsubou-sensei!

00:23:30.110 --> 00:23:32.540
Did everyone draw well?

00:23:32.540 --> 00:23:34.560
Bye bye!
